            <div xml:id="d480">

                <pb facs="0552" n="540" sameAs="frus:frus1943v02/pg540"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">853.79681/101: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-08-05T15:00:00+02:00">August 5, 1943—3
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 3:20 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>5100. Matter dealt with in Department’s 4484, July 26, 8 p.m., was taken up with
                    Foreign Office as instructed. Foreign Office feels, as explained by Lord
                    Halifax, that this matter should be held in abeyance so as not to interfere with
                    certain current negotiations. At a later stage, Foreign Office adds, British
                    Government will be prepared to give us any support it can.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Winant</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
